---
import '../../styles/sim.css';
import '../../styles/sims/gorilla.css';

interface Props {
  label?: string;
}

const { label = 'One viewing · count the passes' } = Astro.props;
---

<gorilla-sim class="sim" data-mode="trial">
  <div class="sim-chrome">
    <span class="sim-chrome-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="sim-chrome-label">{label}</span>
    <span class="sim-chrome-status" data-sim-status aria-live="polite">ready</span>
  </div>

  {/* Two beats. The trial is the single honest viewing; the insight is the
     metacognitive point, and it stays locked until the trial is spent — you
     cannot read why you missed it before you have had your one naive go. */}
  <div class="sim-modes" role="group" aria-label="The trial, then the insight">
    <button type="button" class="sim-mode-tab" data-sim-mode="trial" aria-pressed="true">The trial</button>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="sim-mode-tab"
      data-sim-mode="insight"
      aria-pressed="false"
      disabled
      aria-disabled="true"
      title="Do the trial first — one naive viewing"
    >The insight &#128274;</button>
  </div>

  <div class="sim-panels">
    {/* ── the experiment: one viewing, one count, then the question ── */}
    <section class="sim-panel" data-sim-mode-panel="trial">
      <div class="sim-panel-head">
        <h3 class="sim-panel-title">The task</h3>
      </div>

      <div
        class="sim-stage gor-stage"
        data-sim-court
        role="img"
        aria-label="A court, ready. Three players in white and three in dark will pass a ball; count the passes made by the white team."
      >
        <p class="gor-brief">
          Three players in white pass a ball between themselves, three in dark do the same.
          <b>Count the passes made by the white team.</b> It runs for sixteen seconds and you get one
          go at it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="sim-lead" data-sim-lead aria-live="polite">
        One viewing, and the counting task is real. When you are ready, start the clip and count the
        white team's passes — nothing else is being asked of you.
      </p>

      <div class="gor-row" data-sim-count-row hidden>
        <input
          class="gor-input"
          type="number"
          min="0"
          max="99"
          inputmode="numeric"
          data-sim-count
          placeholder="passes"
          aria-label="How many passes did the white team make?"
        />
        <button type="button" class="gor-btn" data-sim-submit>That is my count</button>
      </div>

      <div data-sim-saw-row hidden>
        <p class="gor-question">Did you see anything other than the players and the ball?</p>
        <div class="gor-row" style="margin-top:10px">
          <button type="button" class="gor-btn" data-sim-saw="yes">Yes</button>
          <button type="button" class="gor-btn" data-sim-saw="no">No</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="gor-actual" data-sim-actual aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="gor-reveal" data-sim-reveal aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
    </section>

    {/* ── the insight: why half miss it — locked until the trial is spent ── */}
    <section class="sim-panel" data-sim-mode-panel="insight" hidden>
      <div class="sim-panel-head">
        <h3 class="sim-panel-title">Why half miss it</h3>
      </div>

      <p class="sim-lead" data-sim-insight-lead aria-live="polite">
        Attention has to be spent on something, and you spent it on the passes. Outside that spotlight
        a person in a gorilla suit could stand in the middle of the frame and beat their chest, and
        for about half of viewers it never reaches awareness at all.
      </p>

      <div class="gor-gap" aria-label="The confidence gap">
        <div class="sim-metric">
          <p class="sim-metric-label">Sure they would have noticed</p>
          <div class="sim-meter"><i class="gor-meter-sure" style="width:94%"></i></div>
          <p class="sim-metric-word">Told afterward, almost everyone is certain a gorilla could not have slipped past them.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sim-metric">
          <p class="sim-metric-label">Actually noticed, first naive viewing</p>
          <div class="sim-meter"><i class="gor-meter-real" style="width:50%"></i></div>
          <p class="sim-metric-word">About half do. The other half were looking right at it and saw nothing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="sim-note">The distance between those two bars is the finding. "I was looking right at it" is no evidence you saw it.</p>

      <div class="gor-load" aria-label="How load changes who misses it">
        <div class="gor-load-bars">
          <div class="gor-load-col">
            <div class="gor-load-track"><i style="height:50%"></i></div>
            <span class="gor-load-word">about half</span>
            <span class="gor-load-cap">count the white team</span>
          </div>
          <div class="gor-load-col">
            <div class="gor-load-track"><i style="height:32%"></i></div>
            <span class="gor-load-word">fewer</span>
            <span class="gor-load-cap">harder count</span>
          </div>
          <div class="gor-load-col">
            <div class="gor-load-track"><i class="is-warm" style="height:72%"></i></div>
            <span class="gor-load-word">most</span>
            <span class="gor-load-cap">attend the dark team</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="gor-load-axis">share who notice the gorilla</p>
      </div>

      <p class="sim-verdict" data-sim-insight-verdict>
        Load decides it. Make the count harder and more people miss the gorilla; track the team whose
        colour matches the gorilla and more people catch it. It is not effort or eyesight — it is where
        the attention went. Half of people were pointed away from it by the very task they were doing well.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  {/* the action bar is rebuilt per mode and phase; the insight beat has none */}
  <div class="sim-controls" data-sim-controls></div>
</gorilla-sim>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/sims/gorilla';
</script>
